From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: dispcc-sm8750: keep the MDSS GDSC on

Once mdss_gdsc collapses, the first DSI bring-up afterwards times out on
the panel init commands and leaves the DSI command engine busy, so every
later frame times out as well; system resume can block in dpm_complete.
Reproduced on the AYN Odin 3 without system suspend: with the display
subsystem runtime-suspended and resumed the display is dead, with it held
active (GDSC on) blank/unblank works every time. Pulsing
DISP_CC_MDSS_CORE_BCR straight after power-on does not help; a pulse
after the failed bring-up lets the next one succeed, so the restore path
itself is incomplete. Until that is fixed, keep the domain on, which is
what effectively happened before the display clock controller reached
sync_state.

---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm8750.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm8750.c
index 18e86b80e581..37a34e687e87 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm8750.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm8750.c
@@ -1759,7 +1759,13 @@ static struct gdsc mdss_gdsc = {
 		.name = "mdss_gdsc",
 	},
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
-	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | HW_CTRL | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
+	/*
+	 * The display does not survive this domain collapsing: the first DSI
+	 * bring-up afterwards leaves the command engine stuck, and only a
+	 * core reset after that failed attempt lets a second one work. Keep
+	 * it on until the DSI restore path is fixed.
+	 */
+	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | HW_CTRL | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE | ALWAYS_ON,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc mdss_int2_gdsc = {
